# Run Environment and Product Requirements

When discussing or implementing **run environment**, **deployment** (Mac vs Linux), **monitoring**, or **control** of the daemon:

- **Run environment & deployment constraints**: read and follow **docs/ARCHITECTURE.md** §2（运行环境与部署约束）. That section defines: TWS runs on two dedicated Mac Minis (Host + Secondary accounts); Prod full stack (Engine, Server, Redis, Celery) on a Linux server connecting to TWS via LAN; Dev stack on local Mac connecting to a separate Dev database; PostgreSQL Dev/Prod isolation on a shared DB server (§2.8, R-DV1); single process on daemon host; monitoring/control logically decoupled (same or separate host); LAN-only monitoring; daemon behavior when IB is unavailable (WAITING_IB, retry, yellow lamp); TWS shared between Dev/Prod with distinct client_id and Engine mutual exclusion (R-DV3).
- **Product requirements** (what to build for monitoring/control, R-M*/R-C*/R-H*/R-B*/R-A*/R-DV*): read **docs/REQUIREMENTS.md**. Capability progress and gaps: **docs/plans/CAPABILITY_TRACKING.md**.

The former is part of system architecture; the latter is independent of run environment (except R-DV* which bridges both).
